## Consequences

(+) `cloud-itonami-isic-5911` now has a real, tested implementation
matching the shape of every other cloud-itonami ISIC actor, replacing a
`:spec` placeholder pointing at a repo that never existed.

(+) `kotoba-lang/industry` registry `\"5911\"` entry promoted to
`:maturity :implemented`.

(+) This actor is another concrete example of Wave 4's person-facing-
service safety guardrail applied to a distinct sensitive-decision axis:
on-set physical-safety/talent-welfare authority (stunt clearance,
minor-performer work-hour limits) rather than clinical-care or
editorial-content authority, all folded into one unconditional
scope-exclusion check that never trusts the advisor's own framing of
its intent, and phrased from the start as finalization-ACTION terms
(not bare nouns) to avoid the fleet-known self-tripping bug class.

(-) Still a simulation/proposal layer, not a real production-management
system. On-set safety-clearance decisions, minor-performer work-hour
compliance, and equipment actuation remain human-/institution-
controlled via external channels.

(-) No integration with real production-management systems (call sheet/
scheduling software, insurance/COI tracking, SAG-AFTRA/union
compliance systems, dailies/DIT pipelines) -- this is a standalone
coordinator blueprint, matching every prior sibling actor's own stated
limitation.

## Alternatives considered

| Option | Verdict | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| Bundle on-set safety clearance as an always-escalate op the actor can still draft | ❌ | Wave 4's guardrail requires that no op directly finalize an on-set-safety-authority decision; even an escalate-only \"draft a stunt clearance\" op would imply the actor participates in constructing that decision, so it is excluded entirely via the closed op allowlist plus the HARD scope-exclusion check, not merely gated |
| Phrase scope-exclusion terms as bare nouns (\"stunt\", \"minor\") for simplicity | ❌ | Directly the fleet-known self-tripping bug class -- a legitimate `:flag-onset-safety-concern` proposal must be free to say \"stunt\" when reporting a real stunt-risk observation; phrasing exclusions as the finalization ACTION avoids the collision structurally |
| Keep `cloud-itonami-isic-5911` at `:spec` only | ❌ | Wave 4 is actively building out the human-facing-services fleet in parallel with Wave 3; this class was unclaimed and ready for a fresh scaffold, mirroring the now-standard `cloud-itonami-isic-873` shape |

